# Part A — Web applications (static & SPA)

# Web Applications (Static & SPA)

**Intent:** Ship, test, and host marketing or product web apps and **host vendored client bundles** (e.g. games). Cross-surface UI policy lives in `product-excellence.mdc` §2a. Game engines and replay logic live in `create-web-game.mdc`. **Simplification passes** (cut copy, chrome, redundancy) → this rule § Simplification + `incubation.mdc` Mode A.

**Applicability:** If a section's `[applicable if …]` does not match your product, **skip the entire section** — do not copy proxy, editor, or ingest patterns onto simple marketing sites.

## Docs map **[core]**

| Doc | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `README.md` | Dev commands, deploy targets, design philosophy |
| `design_spec.md` / `design_specification.md` / `roadmap.md` | Product direction, paused features (e.g. monetization flags) |
| `wrangler.jsonc` / `vercel.json` | Host-specific routing (only the file for your target) |

Read before large changes.

## Stack-agnostic defaults **[core]**

- Prefer **static-first**: content as JSON or markdown under `public/`; minimal server logic.
- Document routing (hash-based or path-based) in README so agents do not guess.
- Global styling: one source of truth (`style.css` or design tokens); if using Tailwind, decide whether preflight is on or off and stay consistent.
- **Monetization:** use explicit feature flags or a documented “monetization paused” constant — do not half-enable paywalls without updating `roadmap.md`.

## UI expectations (web-specific) **[core]**

Visual and accessibility policy → `product-excellence.mdc` §1b (Rams) and §2a. Web-only: keep one global style source (`style.css` or tokens); document tokens in `design_spec.md` when used. Design-only polish (no new routes or behavior) → `incubation.mdc` Mode A before claiming UI done.

## Simplification & copy economy **[core]**

One job per screen. If the user can infer it from layout, **do not label it again in prose**. Run this audit before claiming UI done (pairs with `incubation.mdc` Mode A).

### Copy source of truth

- **Centralize visible strings** in one module (e.g. `src/lib/i18n.js`, `copy.ts`) — EN + any locale variants. Components consume `t(lang).key`; avoid hardcoded marketing paragraphs in JSX.
- **SEO vs UI:** longer keyword copy may live in `index.html`, `seo.js`, or prerender landings — **not** duplicated in the hero, trust bar, and three-column “SEO grids” on the same viewport.
- **Data vs display:** JSON can hold rich hints; the UI may show **caps** (max bullets, max chars) via formatters — trim at display, then shorten source data in a follow-up if still noisy.

### Redundancy audit

Ask for every line of text on a route:

| Question | If yes → |
|----------|----------|
| Is this fact shown elsewhere on the same viewport? | Remove the duplicate (keep one source of truth). |
| Is this the same pitch in hero + trust bar + footer + 3 feature cards? | **One headline + one subline** on the MDP; trust bar = one short line or logos only. |
| Is this a collapsed/closed section with no visible payoff? | Open by default with real content, or **delete** the section. |
| Is this geographic, aspirational, or “studio” fluff on a tool page? | Cut or move to a tertiary route — not footer chrome on the MDP. |
| Is this engineering status dressed as user copy? | Hide when idle; show only during incomplete work (e.g. “Analyzing…”). |
| Are there two cards for one concept (e.g. “Blueprint” + “Signals”)? | **Merge into one card** with one eyebrow label. |

**Anti-patterns (seen in production):**

- Hero H1 + subline + **three SEO columns** restating company tags (same page).
- Same chapter name in header, sidebar tab, and main panel heading.
- Same photo count in stats line, sidebar badge, grid header, and download button label.
- Trust copy in hero + floating strip + footer (pick **one** surface + `/privacy` link).
- Pattern detail: **Trigger / Constraint / Win** labels plus a separate **Signals** box with overlapping bullets.
- Pattern detail: pattern name in page title **and** again inside the guide card.
- Brand wordmark run together (`BRANDNAME`) — use explicit word spacing in a shared `BrandLogo` component.
- Footer with three columns repeating nav + location + taglines the header already implies.
- List/grid cards with long descriptions when **name + count + CTA** suffices.

### Hero & trust (marketing / tool MDP) **[applicable if landing + app tabs share one shell]**

- **Hero:** one H1 + one subline (≤ ~12 words each when possible). No feature grid under the hero unless each card opens distinct content not visible elsewhere.
- **Trust bar:** logos **or** one metrics line — not both repeating the hero pitch.
- **Tabs / primary nav:** labels only; no paragraph under every tab on first paint.
- **Curated path cards**: title + **three-word** subtitle max — or title only.

### Detail pages & reference content **[applicable if cheat sheets, patterns, chapters, docs]**

Use **one card per concept**, identical structure across all items:

```text
[EYEBROW — one word, e.g. Pattern / Chapter]
[optional media — GIF/diagram, sized for readability]
[one gist line — trigger → outcome, no field labels]
[· up to 2 cues — short bullets, not paragraphs]
[template / code block — if applicable]
[list of items — problems, links, etc.]
```

Rules:

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| One eyebrow (`Pattern`, `Chapter`) | Separate “Blueprint”, “Signals”, “More signals” boxes |
| Gist: `{trigger} → {win}` in one line | Labeled rows for Trigger / Constraint / Win |
| Show **≤ 2** cues; cap ~90 chars each in UI | Dump full `howToIdentify` arrays on page |
| Cap gist ~140 chars in formatter | Multi-sentence intro before the list |
| Page `<h1>`/`h2` holds the name | Repeat name inside the guide card |
| Same component for all items | Per-pattern layout forks |

Implement via a shared component + props (`blueprint`, `signals`, `visual`) and constants (`MAX_CUES`, `MAX_GIST_CHARS`). Unit-test formatters.

**List pages:** grid cards = **title + metadata** (count, badge) — drop redundant descriptions when the title is self-explanatory.

### FAQ, About, legal

- **FAQ:** ≤ 4–6 questions; **one-line answers**. Cut overlapping questions.
- **About:** one paragraph + optional quote + stats — not three story paragraphs + disclaimer + quote.
- **Privacy / Terms:** plain-language essentials; avoid repeating the same disclaimer in footer, about, and legal.

### Free tiers & tool directories **[applicable if affiliate / resource lists]**

- Section header: eyebrow + title + **one** subtitle per band (Free vs Pro).
- Tool cards: **name + eligibility badge + CTA** — drop taglines when the name is clear; hide long “how we use it” lists on card face (link out or `<details>` if truly needed).
- Dividers between bands: one short line (`Need paid tools →`), not a paragraph.

### Header chrome (multi-tab apps)

- Single row: **logo `shrink-0` · nav `flex-1 min-w-0` (scroll) · lang + theme `ml-auto shrink-0`**.
- Avoid `absolute` controls overlapping nav on mobile.
- Theme default: explicit in app state (e.g. `'default'`), not an aesthetic preference baked in without product reason.

### Routing & blank screens **[applicable if hash + path SEO landings]**

- If `maybeRedirectLegacyHash()` (or equivalent) runs **before** React mount and returns `true`, the app **never renders** — blank screen with no console error.
- **Fix:** when `pathname` already equals the canonical path, **return false** even if the hash has sub-routes.
- Add E2E for canonical path + hash sub-routes after any redirect refactor.

### Attribution & vendored media

- Local / anonymous assets: **no** author name or article links in UI unless legally required.
- Third-party (e.g. Wikimedia): **Commons + optional Wikipedia overview** — not personal Medium/blog attribution mixed into pattern guides.

### Brand & chrome

- **Wordmark:** multi-word names get visible space, not concatenated spans. One shared component for header + footer.
- **Header:** logo `shrink-0` left; primary CTA right; `justify-between` + explicit `gap` — nav must not crowd the mark.
- **Footer (tool-first sites):** two columns max — brand blurb + contact email; short Explore list (Designer, How it works, Privacy). One copyright line. No location pins unless the product is *about* place.
- **Buttons:** one geometric language per tier (e.g. primary CTAs all `rounded-full`); do not mix pill and boxy on the same funnel step.

### Idle onboarding (paste / upload flows)

- **Narrow reading column** (`max-w-2xl` / `max-w-3xl`) — not full-bleed empty canvas.
- **Hero stack:** job statement → single trust line (Privacy · process modal) → form. No sixth text layer.
- **Sample / demo output:** show real thumbnails **inline** or omit entirely. Never a closed `<details>` that only shows a headline — users read it as broken.
- **Remove** sidebar placeholders that restate what the main panel already does.

### Workspace stats (one calm line)

When users ingest batches (folders, galleries), expose **numbers only** in one `role="status"` line under the title:

```text
43 in folder · 31 shown · 9 duplicates hidden · 3 blur filtered · 4 selected
```

Rules:

- Always: `N in folder · M shown`.
- Append segments **only when > 0** (duplicates, blur-filtered, excluded, selected).
- During async work: replace with `Analyzing…` or `Layout 12/43` — not the full stats string.
- Implement via a pure formatter (e.g. `formatWorkspaceStats()`) + unit tests; do not scatter string templates in JSX.
- Full breakdown belongs in **settings / curation dialog**, not repeated in the grid header.

### Progressive disclosure that earns its keep

- **Good:** Export PDF primary; Edit folder + Curation + Analyze batch in overflow `⋯`.
- **Good:** Advanced thresholds inside collapsed `<details>` in a dialog.
- **Bad:** Icon tabs plus a text heading repeating the tab name plus instructional microcopy for obvious interactions (“Click to select”).
- **Bad:** Stats line when nothing is in progress and every number is duplicated elsewhere.

### Verification for simplification **[core]**

- Desktop + mobile screenshot: can a new user name the **one** primary action in 3 seconds?
- Count distinct places the same noun appears — **≤ 2** per viewport.
- Pattern/detail routes: exactly **one** guide card above the list; no `Trigger:` labels in DOM.
- E2E smoke: assert stable copy on routes you keep; **remove** assertions for deleted boilerplate; update `page-objects` hero patterns when H1 changes.
- After copy pass: run `npm test` + spot-check `/patterns#…/pattern/…` (or equivalent deep link) for blank-screen regressions.

## SPA resilience & SEO **[core]**

- **Error boundaries:** route- or section-level fallback UI with retry/home — never a blank screen on render failure.
- **Code splitting:** lazy-load heavy routes (games, admin, charts) via dynamic `import()` or framework equivalent.
- **Shareable UI state `[applicable if filters/tabs/search should be linkable]`:** put bookmarkable state in URL hash or query params — not ephemeral UI (modals, scroll, drafts) or sensitive values.
- **SEO (per route):** unique `<title>`, meta description, canonical URL, Open Graph tags — even for hash routes, set document title on navigation.
- **Third-party scripts & CSP `[applicable if you add external trackers/widgets]`:** update CSP to match what you actually load — do not add analytics by default; if you do add a tracker, allowlist its domains explicitly (avoid `'unsafe-inline'` / `'unsafe-eval'` unless your bundler requires them).
- **`[applicable if TypeScript]`** enable `strict`; prefer `unknown` over `any`.

## Performance & Optimization **[core]**

- **Core Web Vitals (CWV):** Monitor and optimize for LCP (Largest Contentful Paint), INP (Interaction to Next Paint), and CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift).
- **Asset & Image Optimization:** Use modern image formats (WebP/AVIF), provide responsive `srcset`, and use `loading="lazy"` for off-screen media.
- **Progressive Web App (PWA):** `[applicable if offline capable]` Implement Service Workers using reliable caching strategies (e.g., stale-while-revalidate for assets, network-first for data) to provide resilient offline/flaky-network experiences.

## SPA hosting **[core]**

- Production build outputs to `dist/` (or equivalent).
- **Cloudflare Workers / static assets:** `assets.directory` → `./dist`, `not_found_handling: single-page-application` so unknown paths fall back to `index.html`.
- **Vercel / Netlify:** equivalent SPA rewrite rules in host config.
- **Dev server:** if you vend a nested client SPA under `public/<app>/`, mirror SPA fallback in Vite (or host) preview so deep links work locally — not only in production.

**DSA Patterns production deploy** → § *DSA Patterns site* below (Wrangler upload, CDN purge, `main`/`master` mirror).

## Thin server on static apps **[applicable if Workers/API routes proxy third-party URLs or ingest user links]**

Static-first does not mean zero server logic. When you add a **fetch proxy** or **link-ingest** handler (Drive folders, OG images, etc.), treat it as a shared resource every user hits.

- **Allowlist upstream hosts** — HTTPS only; validate hostname *and* path pattern before `fetch`; re-check after redirects.
- **Upstream timeout** — every outbound `fetch` gets `AbortController` + a strict deadline (e.g. 10s); return **504** on abort; `clearTimeout` in `finally` so hung calls cannot exhaust the connection pool.
- **Rate limit by real client IP** — extract IP in order: `cf-connecting-ip` → first `x-forwarded-for` → `x-real-ip` → `"unknown"`. If deploy omits all headers, every user shares one bucket — document required proxy/CDN headers in README.
- **Same-origin gate for browser proxies `[applicable if open relay abuse is a concern]`** — prefer matching `Origin` or `Referer`; know that strict deny-when-both-missing breaks some privacy browsers and non-browser clients — weigh abuse vs compatibility.
- **Response hygiene** — enforce expected `content-type`, cap body size, use `cache-control: private` for user-specific bytes; generic error messages to clients (log upstream bodies server-side only).
- **Server-side validation mirrors UI** — client regex is UX, not security; reject hostname bypass (e.g. `evil.com/folders/{id}`) in the handler before parsing IDs.
- **Privacy-aligned defaults `[applicable if handling user media/links]`** — prefer client-side export over uploading user media when feasible; avoid PII in telemetry; do not persist user content server-side without a threat model (localStorage/session for prefs, auth, or cart is fine).

Extract shared helpers (`getClientIp`, URL allowlist) into `src/lib/` and unit-test them.
- **Proxied media URLs** — wrap third-party image URLs through one helper (e.g. `proxiedXUrl()`); keep helper and server allowlist in the **same module** with unit tests. When upstream changes hostname/path (e.g. `drive.google.com/thumbnail` vs `lh3.googleusercontent.com`), update both together or thumbnails break silently.

## External link ingest **[applicable if users paste third-party folder/file URLs]**

- **Primary + fallback paths** — API key (full listing) + best-effort fallback (smaller cap); log fallback server-side; toast honest limits to users (~60 vs 500+).
- **Hard caps in code and tests** — max items ingested, folder depth, export batch size; constants referenced in unit tests and `product_spec.md`.
- **Abort long ingest** — server handler timeout (e.g. 60s) separate from per-fetch proxy timeout.

## Editor / workspace routes **[applicable if marketing landing + heavy tool on same site]**

- **Progressive disclosure** — marketing chrome (header, footer) before first success; after success, **hide** site header; compact workspace toolbar. Keep escape hatches (privacy, edit source) in overflow — not a second row of equal-weight buttons.
- **One primary action per workspace** — e.g. Export PDF filled; Download only when selection &gt; 0; everything else in `⋯` menu or Curation dialog.
- **One stats line** — see § Simplification → Workspace stats; never restate counts in sidebar, grid header, and toolbar.
- **Sidebar vs main** — sidebar = chapter list + mode icons (spreads/photos); main = content only. No dashed placeholder in sidebar when the grid lives in main.
- **Main panel headings** — drop redundant chapter suffix when chapter is highlighted in sidebar; photos view needs no “Photos / Chapter / N photos · click to…” block — actions only (Select all / Clear).
- **Contextual inspector `[applicable if complex editor]`** — right rail shows one context (cover, caption); instructional paragraphs → `sr-only` or dialog.
- **Mobile tool nav `[applicable if editor has a side rail]`** — vertical rail → bottom filmstrip; pad main content above fixed nav.
- **Human labels** — map internal enums to plain language (`blur filtered` not `filtered`; `duplicates hidden` not internal scorer jargon).

## Trust UX for user-supplied input **[applicable if users paste links or run client-heavy export]**

- **Process modal `[applicable if server reads user links/files]`** — deep trust dive in one modal; hero gets a single inline link (Privacy · How we process…). No third floating trust strip above the footer.
- **Inline errors** — map domain failures (private link, timeout, rate limit) via a formatter; add one recovery hint; never stack traces.
- **Client-heavy export `[applicable if PDF/canvas/render in browser]`** — detect OOM/memory failures and suggest recovery (fewer items, close tabs, split batches).
- **Demo/sample output `[applicable if paste-or-upload onboarding]`** — optional **visible** sample row on landing; on the tool route, prefer doing the real job over sample chrome. If samples exist, they must be visible without a click — otherwise remove.

## Hosting vendored sub-apps **[core]**

When embedding a separate client build (games, tools):

1. Upstream build sets correct **asset `base`** subpath.
2. Copy artifacts to `public/<app-id>/` with `index.html` at folder root.
3. Host SPA fallback for `/public-path/*` client routes (host config + dev middleware).
4. Optional theme overlay CSS on parent chrome for contrast when iframe'd.
5. **`[applicable if parent host is static-only]`** Static parent cannot run your Worker/API — ship embed/preview mode with mocked ingest; document that live third-party calls need full deploy + secrets. Hidden previews: `noindex`, omit from sitemap; sync script in parent repo after vendoring.
6. For game-specific iframe height, embed detection, and engine rules → `create-web-game.mdc`.

## Verification gate **[core]**

Before claiming done:

```bash
npm test
npm run build
npm run test:e2e   # when present
```

- Structural/data tests under `tests/` when applicable.
- **E2E smoke:** extend route list when adding hash or path pages; assert **stable copy** on each route.
- Prefer **accessible role + name** for E2E selectors; use `data-testid` only when roles are ambiguous; reset state in `beforeEach`.
- **Network mocking `[applicable if third-party APIs in CI]`:** use `page.route` / `cy.intercept` or env flags so CI stays deterministic.
- **Funnel E2E `[applicable if multi-step submit → export flow]`:** one spec for the happy path, not only per-route smoke.
- **Manual runbook `[applicable if CI mocks external APIs]`:** optional `teste2e.md` with real credentials for pre-release QA; keep CI mocked.
- After changing vendored assets under `public/`, run full build so `dist/` matches.

## Git & deploy **[core]**

- **Canonical branch:** prefer `main`; if the remote still mirrors **`master`**, keep aligned: `git push origin main` then `git push origin main:master` when your workflow references both.
- After deploy, if users see stale shells: purge CDN cache for `/` and `/assets/*` (and `/games/*` when vendored embeds changed), hard-refresh; confirm latest CI deploy succeeded.

## Static Portal Site Integration **[applicable if hosting embedded apps/games]**

**Project map** for agents working in static host portals. Embedded sub-apps → §12 (*Host site integration*).

### Authoritative docs (read before large changes)

| Doc | Use for |
|-----|--------|
| `README.md` | Dev commands, deployment targets, Capacitor/PWA config, testing, design philosophy |
| Host routing config | Cloudflare Workers (`wrangler.jsonc`) or Vercel (`vercel.json`) SPA routing |
| `design_specification.md` | Static-first React, CSS tokens, component architecture |
| `roadmap.md` | Product direction and paused features |

### Stack and structure

- **Framework:** React / Vite / static HTML.
- **Routing:** Hash-based or path-based SPA routing.
- **Data:** Static JSON under `public/data/` or asset bundles under `public/games/<slug>/`.

### UI and UX (site-specific)

- **Design philosophy:** Simplicity, edge-to-edge readability, calm typography; avoid visual noise.
- **Themes:** Standardize on high-contrast Default and Dark/Midnight themes using CSS tokens.
- **Accessibility:** Preserve `:focus-visible` focus indicators and keyboard navigation.

### Monetization and premium code

- **Monetization paused:** Search `MONETIZATION_PAUSED` in components when toggling paywalls/pricing.

### Verification & Deployment

```bash
npm test
npm run build
npm run test:e2e
```

- **Git integration:** Treat `main` as source of truth; fast-forward `master` when both exist (`git merge --ff-only`).
- **CDN cache:** Purge CDN cache for `/` and asset subpaths after deploying static updates.

