# Part B — Game development

# Game Development

**Intent:** Build any game genre (action, puzzle, idle, narrative) with optional determinism, embeds, and PWA — not general marketing site routing (see `create-web-game.mdc`). UI policy on all surfaces → `product-excellence.mdc` §2a.

**Tag legend:** **[core]** every game should consider; **[applicable if …]** skip when irrelevant (e.g. do not force netcode rules on a casual puzzle).

## §1 Product locks before scale **[core]**

- Lock **visual direction**, **monetization ethics** (e.g. cosmetics-only, no pay-to-win), and **renderer/runtime** early. Name the **nearest genre reference** for UI/HUD (e.g. 2048 for tile puzzles, classic brawlers for fighters) — see `product-excellence.mdc` §2d.
- Record **ADRs** in `docs/decisions/` so future agents know *why*, not only *what*.
- **`[applicable if public roster / real-world names]`** — legal/name checklist before scaling content (trademark, slurs, restricted names).
- **`[applicable if freemium]`** — document DLC scope; never sell gameplay power.

## §1b Product design craft **[core]**

Systems and feel before feature lists. Prefer Cursor agents `@game-designer`, `@level-designer`, `@narrative-designer`, `@technical-artist`, `@game-audio-engineer` when authoring GDDs or levels; keep this rule as the engineering checklist.

- **Design pillars** — lock 3–5 non-negotiable player experiences before adding features; every mechanic must serve at least one pillar.
- **Three-loop model** — document moment-to-moment (0–30s), session (5–30 min), and long-term (hours–weeks) loops. For puzzle embeds: solve beat → session of N levels → campaign/meta progression.
- **Time pressure policy** — Blitz/time-attack modes are excellent hooks for active puzzles, but must **never** be forced onto meditative titles where they cause cognitive overload.
- **Mechanic spec minimum** — for each core mechanic: purpose, player fantasy, inputs/outputs, success and failure states, edge cases, tuning levers. Mark unplaytested numbers `[PLACEHOLDER]` until validated.
- **Onboarding checklist** — core verb within ~30s of first control; first success guaranteed; each new mechanic in low-stakes context; at least one discoverable without wall-of-text; first session ends on a hook (unlock, cliff-hanger, or “one more”).
- **Level / pacing `[applicable if level-based]`** — per level: player fantasy, pacing arc, mechanic taught (spatially when possible), critical-path readability. Ship order: blockout (solvable grey box) → playtest → dress (VFX/audio). Do not art-polish an untested layout.
- **Audio feel `[applicable if SFX/music]`** — every core verb gets a clear sonic cue when audio is on; keep gesture-gated unlock and volume controls per §5; prefer lean WebAudio / procedural SFX when download budget is tight (§3).

## §2 Architecture: engine vs shell **[core]**

- **Pure game core** — no UI framework, no DOM, no `window` in simulation code (`packages/<engine>/` or equivalent).
- **Presentation shell** — menu routes in your web framework; Canvas/WebGL/DOM renderer **reads** core state only.
- **Versioned schemas** for entities, levels, and events so saves and replays survive refactors.

**`[applicable if action / fighting / sports / deterministic replay]`**

- **Fixed timestep** sim (e.g. 60 Hz) in core; render may interpolate.
- **Deterministic math** — fixed-point or integer-only physics; avoid raw floats for authoritative state.
- **Seeded PRNG** — all gameplay randomness from a seed stored with the replay.
- **Input ring buffer** — early presses still register within a small window.
- **Central feel module** — hitstop, shake, freeze frames in one place for designers and replay parity.
- **Replay = inputs + seed**; automated verify must reproduce identical outcomes before claiming netcode-ready.

**`[applicable if puzzle / turn-based / low stakes]`**

- Determinism optional; still separate **solver/level data** from UI; document algorithms honestly for educational hosts.

## §3 Renderer & assets **[core]**

- Pick renderer for **lowest common device** (Canvas 2D, DOM, SVG) unless you need WebGL **`[applicable if 3D or heavy particles]`**.
- Document renderer choice in an ADR (Canvas for broad mobile support vs WebGL for effects — project decides).
- **`[applicable if zero-download audio]`** — WebAudio synth / procedural SFX.
- **`[applicable if large asset pipeline]`** — lazy load, cache strategy, mobile size budget.
- **`[applicable if action / many spawned entities]`** — object pooling for bullets/particles; target ~**16 ms** sim slice per frame on low-end mobile.

## §4 Screens, embeds, and host sites **[core]**

Stand-alone PWA **or** iframe on a parent site:

- Detect embed: `window.self !== window.top` → compact layout class on `<html>` (project-defined prefix).
- **Iframe / shell height** — `clamp()` / `dvh` floors so menus and CTAs are not clipped; `@media (max-height: …)` fallback.
- **Touch** — minimum targets; on-screen controls when keyboard unavailable **`[applicable if mobile browser]`**.
- **`[applicable if portrait-first mobile]`** — dedicated HUD pass (after core loop is fun on landscape/desktop).
- **Host vendoring** — build with correct `base` subpath → copy to `public/games/<id>/` → host SPA fallback → theme overlay CSS for parent contrast.
- **`[applicable if educational host]`** — short note naming real algorithms used (accurate labels only).

Host routing details → `create-web-game.mdc` (vendored folder only).

## §5 Player experience baseline **[core]**

- Remappable controls + persisted settings **`[applicable if keyboard/gamepad]`**.
- Pause that **stops the simulation tick**, not only hides UI.
- Live audio sliders (master / SFX / music).
- In-match reference UI (moves, objectives) for onboarding.
- Local settings + progress in `localStorage` / IndexedDB **`[applicable if client-only]`**.
- **Micro-Celebrations & Juice** — Sync the "Holy Trinity" of game feel on core verbs: Visual pop + Audio chord + Haptic vibration.
- **Win States & Continuous Blitz Flow** — Avoid static "Solved." text. Require tally count-ups and particle bursts (respecting `prefers-reduced-motion`). In **Blitz/timed rush modes**, remove mid-run "Next" buttons—let dwell timers auto-advance levels continuously while showing non-blocking solve toasts.
- **Session Completion & Audio Transitions** — On session end (time/lives out), fade background music (BGM) to 0 (silence) and play a dedicated procedural Web Audio chime (`sfxModeComplete` / `sfxTimeUp`) to clearly signal the transition.
- **Auto-Home Navigation & Tap-to-Linger** — When a timed session finishes, trigger a 2-second auto-redirect to Home, but cancel the timer immediately if the player taps the results card so they can linger on their score/stats without being forced off-screen (skip auto-redirect in E2E test mode).

**Game HUD / UI:** apply `product-excellence.mdc` §1b; keep HUD minimal in embeds so play area is not shrunk by ornamental chrome.

## §6 Tools & live ops (client-only) **`[applicable if designer-heavy]`**

- Local telemetry (usage, win rates) — on-device, privacy-first.
- Tuning overlay writing to local storage without redeploy for every tweak.
- Hidden admin or `noindex` QA routes; keep player navigation clean.

## §7 Delivery & hardening **[core]**

- **`[applicable if offline / installable]`** — PWA with documented SW strategy; on embed subpaths, scope or disable SW so the **parent site's** service worker and routing are not hijacked — test both standalone and iframe before ship.
- No debug globals exposing solver, full state, or level data in production; build verify fails if reintroduced.
- Minify shipped client JS; `drop_console` where appropriate; README states client bundles are not secret — license + server validation when cheating matters (deterrence, not secrecy).
- **`[applicable if TanStack CSR embed suite]`** — Bharat `build-all-embeds.mjs` uses esbuild `drop: ['console']`; host `verify-game-dist-cloudflare.mjs` gates shipped assets.
- Test on throttled network once before release.

## §8 Testing & definition of done **[core]**

- E2E (Playwright or equivalent): reach first interactive frame, complete minimal play path, screenshot on critical views.
- **`[applicable if deterministic core]`** — automated replay verification in CI.
- Smoke narrow + wide viewport; test embed and standalone if both ship.
- **`[applicable if level-based puzzle]`** — **one unit test per level** (structure + solvability where provable); shared `level-count.test.mjs` asserting N levels in source; update E2E copy when total level count changes (e.g. `Puzzle 1 / 30` for Echo, `/ 20` for most suite games — never stale `/ 3` or `/ 15`).
- **`[applicable if embed iframe on educational host]`** — run E2E against local preview server serving `dist/client` at `/games/<slug>/`; keep `?e2e=1` auto-win paths **runtime-only** (never `VITE_E2E` at build — `build-all-embeds.mjs` deletes it); clear `localStorage` progress keys in `beforeEach`; `campaign-5` / smoke matrices follow **current** `EMBED_GAMES` (+ inlined mode routes for archived fantasies); fast and deterministic (instant win when puzzle already solved).

## §12 Embed puzzle suite — production learnings **[applicable if iframe embed on parent SPA]**

Reference implementation: CSR games vendored to `public/games/<slug>/` on a static host SPA. Catalog single source of truth → `scripts/games/embed-registry.mjs`.

### Embed inventory management

- Maintain a central `EMBED_GAMES` registry as the single source of truth.
- Soft-archived standalones live as **inlined modes** (e.g. `/modes/<name>`) rather than separate hub cards or distinct host trees.
- Slugs must remain stable for bookmarks and CDN caching.

### Viral hooks (client-only — no server leaderboards)

Copy templates from `scripts/games/templates/` into each game's `src/lib/`:

- `dailySeed.ts` + `?daily=1` — deterministic daily puzzle.
- `shareResult.ts` + `shareOverlay.css` — emoji/OG share cards on win.
- `localBest.ts` — local PB ghost replay.
- `progress.ts` — campaign persist (`<slug>.progress` in `localStorage`).
- **Percentiles over Raw Ranks** — For daily or global modes, use math-based percentile distributions (e.g. "You beat 84% of players") rather than live leaderboards, as low-traffic live leaderboards look like "empty rooms".

### Theme switcher integration

- Import theme CSS templates **before** framework base utilities so CSS variables take precedence.
- Ensure theme switcher controls do not overlap interactive play area trays or bottom navigation bars.

### Host site integration

Vendored static bundles live under `public/games/<slug>/`.

#### Outer iframe shell (host)

- **Width:** Responsive cap on the games column (`60vw`, `max-w-[900px]`, centered).
- **Height:** Stable block so in-iframe CTAs / mode lobbies are not clipped. Prefer `h-[clamp(…)]` / `100dvh` floors; tune per title after screenshot testing on mobile viewports.
- **`iframeSrc` — lobby roots only:** Always use `'/games/<slug>/'` (trailing slash). Never point hub iframe to deep client routes like `/play` or `/campaign`.

#### Tutorial UX inside the iframe (game-side)

- Detect iframe early: `window.self !== window.top` → add compact class on `<html>` to adapt layout for smaller viewports.
- Primary CTAs (Next, Start, Retry) must remain reachable above the fold.

### Audio: SFX vs BGM

- **SFX** — WebAudio oscillators, haptics, slow-mo on solve. Call `unlockSfx()` on first user gesture.
- **BGM** — Separate from SFX. Use looping HTML Audio or procedural step-sequencer loops.
- `duckBgm()` on win overlay; `stopBgm()` on route unmount.

### Generic Game Feel & Logic Learnings

- **Win celebrate vs `prefers-reduced-motion`:** If reduced-motion dwell equals (or is shorter than) the solve-hold before chrome mounts, the win overlay never paints. Keep celebrate visibility (≥ ~2–4s) independent of reduced motion settings.
- **Web Share API (`navigator.share`) vs Clipboard:** Avoid silent fallbacks to clipboard. If native share isn't supported, provide explicit, separate "Copy Link" and "Share" buttons.
- **Physics-Based CPU Opponents:** Use **Monte-Carlo simulation** during CPU turns (running the deterministic loop headlessly 50-100 times with random variation) rather than complex analytical math.
- **Difficulty budgets with flat penalties:** Use a hybrid formula `(Cost * Multiplier) + Flat Armor` so short levels aren't instantly failed by a single flat penalty.

